%% The widget declarations of CSSN's mini-app (vGLP, Section 6.2, Definition "Widget Declaration"), as the apps of GSC's contracts and GAI's declare theirs (programs/apps/<app>/self.vglp), in the words Udi gave for CSSN's Figure 3 (reported by CSSN #8 Cowork, Code_inbox.md, 2026-10-20 10:10 UTC): the approval question of its platform, Approval, drawn by the construct family's approval_sentence, one sentence for the attempt's class and two buttons labelled for it; and its request question, Menu, drawn by the construct family's social_menu with the last state on construct 0, each person with what the state says of them and the requests the person composes (glp_multiagent/lib/ui_runtime/named_widgets.dart and tab_screen.dart).  They are the app's, not the platform's: platform.vglp stays as compile.sh prints it from CSSN.glp, with its own declaration for its output, Stream(Output) =::= last_state.
Approval =::= approval_sentence.
Menu =::= social_menu.
